<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "http://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">

<!-- ===========================================================================================
     TWO INDEPENDENT PARALLELISM AXES. Read both before changing either.

       thread-count="1"                 - how many <test> BLOCKS run at once. One, so the blocks
                                          below run one after another. Covered by 1 and 2 below.
       data-provider-thread-count="5"   - how many SCENARIOS run at once INSIDE one block. Five.
                                          Covered by 3 below: shares one account per block, which
                                          rule 2 forbids, but measured on qa and did not reproduce.

     Setting thread-count to 1 does not make this suite serial. The two multiply: one block at a
     time, five scenarios in flight within it.

     THIS IS A CAPACITY DECISION, NOT A CORRECTNESS ONE - and that is a change from before.
     The two things that used to make parallelism unsafe are both resolved (see 1 and 2 below),
     so the only remaining limit is the machine. Selenium sizes a node's Chrome slots from the
     CPU count, and the Jenkins agent's own node log says:

         [NodeOptions.getSessionFactories] Detected 2 available processors
         [NodeOptions.report] Adding Chrome for {"browserName": "chrome", ...} 2 times

     Two slots. At thread-count 5 the three surplus sessions never started, and because Sauron's
     ScreenshotBddListener then throws on the absent driver, every one of those scenarios reported
     "Driver not initialized. Is @WebTest/@MobileTest missing on class/method?" - naming neither
     the browser nor the real cause. Build #234 lost roughly three scenarios in five that way.

     RAISING IT AGAIN: the ceiling is min(agent CPUs, distinct accounts). On qa there are 7 active
     blocks with 7 distinct accounts, so accounts are not the constraint - cores are. Budget about
     one core and ~1GB of RAM per concurrent session and leave 2 for the build itself, so
     thread-count 5 wants a 7-8 CPU agent, or a remote grid via the Jenkins GRID_URL parameter
     (docker-compose.grid.yml). The Test stage also caps thread-count to the agent's CPU count at
     build time, so an undersized agent degrades to a slower run rather than a false failure.

     Two pieces of shared state used to make BLOCK parallelism unsafe. Both are fixed; read them
     before raising thread-count, because neither protects you if a new block reuses an account.
     Item 3 is the same account-sharing hazard on the OTHER axis - not fixed, but measured, and it
     did not reproduce. Read 3 before trusting 2's stated mechanism; the run in 3 casts doubt on it.

       1. FIXED - assertion state. Hooks.softAssert was "public static SoftAssert", ONE instance
          for the whole JVM: @Before replaced it and @After called assertAll() on it, so with two
          scenarios in flight one wiped the other's collected assertions and failures were
          reported against the wrong scenario or lost outright - a green run that was not green.
          Hooks.softAssert is now a final ThreadLocalSoftAssert: one shared handle, but the
          failures are collected per THREAD, i.e. per scenario in flight. Call sites are
          unchanged. Measured on the pre-fix code with five concurrent scenarios raising three
          failures each, one scenario reported NONE of its own and another reported nine
          belonging to other scenarios; after the fix every scenario reports its own three and no
          foreign ones.

       2. THE STANDING RULE - two blocks that can run at the same time may not share an account.
          CCP logout is SERVER-SIDE and Hooks.afterScenario clicks Log out after EVERY scenario,
          so a second block signed in as the same customer loses its session mid-scenario. The
          symptom is a scatter of "session expired" failures that read as product bugs.

          TestGroupContext is ThreadLocal and every active block below has its own test.group, but
          a group is only as isolated as the credential it resolves to. On qa each active block
          now resolves to a distinct account: Login is testautomation01 (via account.login.*,
          which is what its features actually drive - they never call "ccp login with configured
          user"), and Homepage/Cart/PDP_PLP/SF_SLC_SLO/Profile are on their own jswtest.in
          accounts. tokencheck.user.* is still testautomation01, which is why the TokenCheck block
          below must stay commented out until it has an account of its own.

          NOT TRUE OF PREPROD. This suite pins no environment, so -Denv=preprod runs it at the
          same thread-count, and in global_preprod.properties testautomation01@yopmail.com still
          backs login, cart, homepage, orders and pdpplp - five active blocks on one customer.
          Give preprod its own per-group accounts, or run it serially, before pointing this suite
          at it.

       3. WITHIN-BLOCK ACCOUNT SHARING - the same sharing rule 2 forbids, one layer down. Measured
          rather than reasoned about, and it did NOT reproduce. Kept at 5.

          Why rule 2 does not cover this. Rule 2 is satisfied by giving each <test> BLOCK its own
          account. This axis runs five scenarios of the SAME block concurrently, and they all
          resolve the SAME credential: UserConfig.getEmail() reads the group from TestGroupContext
          and maps it to one <group>.user.email. TestGroupContext being ThreadLocal does not help -
          every thread in a block holds the same group, so it resolves the same account.
          global_qa.properties defines exactly one email/password per group; there is no pool and no
          per-thread variant, and sessions.yaml defines a single ccp session config.

          The axis is live, not inert. Sauron's SauronCucumberTest.scenarios() carries
          @DataProvider(parallel = true) - verified in the bytecode of cucumber-4.0.6-SNAPSHOT.jar,
          where the plain cucumber-testng parent it overrides is NOT parallel. So this setting takes
          effect regardless of thread-count. Confirmed at runtime: five TestNG-PoolService threads,
          five browsers, five concurrent logins as qa_homepage_user.

          MEASURED 2026-09-07, Homepage block on qa, dptc=5. A probe suite carrying only the
          Homepage <test> block, every other parameter copied from this file (selfHeal included):

              44 scenarios - 40 passed, 4 broken, 18m49s
              ZERO session or auth failures: no "session expired", no 401, no unauthorized,
              across roughly 40 logins with 5 in flight on one shared account

          The 4 broken were ordinary locator/timing failures, not eviction: the footer about-us
          link staying on /corporate (x2 of 13 outline examples), a search-to-PDP timeout on
          //a[contains(@href,'/product-detail')], and a NoSuchElementException on the search button.

          So the eviction predicted from rule 2 did not happen on this axis. Two probable reasons,
          and BOTH weaken rule 2's premise rather than this axis specifically:
            - Chrome runs incognito (the "incognito" flag is in Sauron's chromeOptions args), so
              every session has its own cookie jar. Spelled without the leading dashes on purpose:
              a literal double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment and breaks this file.
            - "No log out is found" appeared 20 times in that run, i.e. ccpLogOut() threw and the
              server-side logout never fired at all. Where it did fire it evicted only itself.

          WHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH. One 19-minute run on qa is not proof the mechanism can
          never fire - only that it did not at this concurrency, on this env, in this window. It
          says nothing either way about rule 2's cross-BLOCK claim, which remains untested. And the
          dptc=1 control that would have told us whether those 4 failures are concurrency-induced
          or pre-existing was INVALID: it reported Tests run: 0 after 43m46s and died with
          NoSuchSessionException / UnsupportedCommandException, the grid having degraded mid-run.
          The one signal that survived is that the footer about-us failure appeared in both runs,
          so that one is not concurrency-related. Re-run the control before trusting any pass/fail
          comparison between 1 and 5.

          IF IT EVER DOES BITE, the signature is a scatter of session failures landing in Allure as
          BROKEN, not failed - they throw rather than assert - so check the broken column before
          suspecting the product. The fix would be a per-group account POOL:
          <group>.user.email.1..N with a handout keyed to the executing thread, falling back to the
          single account when no pool is configured. That is credential provisioning before it is
          code - it needs N real accounts per active group and none exist today. The cheap
          alternative is setting this attribute to 1, which is the whole fix and needs no code
          change.
     =========================================================================================== -->
<suite verbose="1" name="Jsw automation" parallel="tests" thread-count="1"
       data-provider-thread-count="5" annotations="JDK">

    <listeners>
        <listener class-name="com.qapitol.jsw.config.TestGroupListener"/>
    </listeners>

    <!-- env / data.env are set by GlobalConfigProperties from -Denv (default: qa).
         Override here only if this suite must pin one environment. -->
    <parameter name="data.testId" value="testCaseId"/>
    <parameter name="api.retry.count" value="1"/>
    <parameter name="enableSessionsKeepAlive" value="true"/>
    <parameter name="executionTimeout" value="10000"/>
    <parameter name="cucumber.publish.quiet" value="true"/>
    <parameter name="cucumber.plugin"
               value="com.qapitol.sauron.report.core.cucumber.CucumberSauronReportEventsProvider"/>
    <parameter name="cucumber.glue" value="com.qapitol.jsw.stepdefinition,com.qapitol.jsw.utils"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal" value="true"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.recovery.tries" value="2"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.score.cap" value="0.7"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.server" value="http://34.47.228.105:7878"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.imitator.server" value="http://34.47.228.105:8000"/>

<!-- ================================ LOGIN ================================ -->

    <test name="Login">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="login"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@login or @registration or @forgetPassword"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <!-- ================================ HOMEPAGE ================================ -->

    <test name="Homepage">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="homepage"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@header or @footer or @blogs or @search"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <test name="PDP_PLP">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="pdpplp"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@PLPValidation or @PDPValidation"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- ================================== CART ================================== -->

    <!-- @AddToCartAndCreateOpportunity is a FEATURE-level tag, so this selects every active
         scenario in AddToCartAndCreateOpportunity.feature, not just the create-opportunity one. -->
    <test name="Cart_AddToCartAndCreateOpportunity">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="cart"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags"
                   value="@AddToCartAndCreateOpportunity"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- =============================== SF ORDERS =============================== -->
    <!-- SFSlc.feature and SFSlo.feature have no Background - they drive Salesforce/API flows
         rather than a browser login - but they still run under the orders group's data. -->

    <test name="SF_SLC_SLO">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="orders"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@slcOrderCreation or @sloOrderCreation"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- ================================= GUEST ================================= -->

    <test name="GuestHomePage">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="Guest"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@GuestUserHomePage"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- =============================== TOKEN CHECK =============================== -->

    <!-- Both token features in one block: LoginUserToken logs in and closes the payment-due
         popup, GuestUserToken only opens the session.
         Runs under its own "tokencheck" group, which resolves to testautomation01@yopmail.com in
         both qa and preprod. It used to share the "profile" group, whose account is a real mailbox
         with a rotating password - that returned HTTP 401 and cost every token scenario in
         CCP_Regression #231. A dedicated group also keeps EmptyBankDetails, Address,
         CustomerDetails, bankDetails and forgetPassword on the profile account, untouched. -->
    <!-- <test name="TokenCheck">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="tokencheck"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@tokenCheckLogin or @tokenCheckGuestUser"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test> -->


    <!-- ================================ PROFILE ================================ -->

    <!-- EmptyBankDetails.feature logs in with credentials hardcoded in its own Background
         ("emailnoti@yopmail.com"), so test.group does not drive authentication here - it is
         set only because TestGroupContext requires a value. -->
    <test name="Profile">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="profile"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@customerDetails or @EmptyBankDetails"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- ===========================================================================================
         Reference: areas NOT included above, with their verified tags. Uncomment the block you
         need, or add the tag to an existing block that already uses the right test.group.

           homepage : @paymentDue  @ledger  @bankDetails  @myAccount  @buym
           cart     : @CartVerification  @shipment  @EditAndDeleteCart  @ccpActiveOrder  @creditOrder
           profile  : @address
           orders   : @ccpErpSyncRegression
           Guest    : @SEOCheck
           api      : @customerProfileApi  @rcv2Api  @centralCart
                      (point cucumber.features at src/test/resources/features/api for these)
         =========================================================================================== -->

</suite>
